  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Atoms see only the port relation",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Atoms see only the port relation (proved for every knot space by an exhaustive finite check extending GLUE-READ A's). Let B be a Fano atom, C its cut facing a removal and R the port relation there; by ticket A, B with its closed sides is the Fano plane minus C's element, up to flips. Feeding at once every deep point of the removal's side and every mixed pair of such a point with a deep point behind another element of B never changes whether creation occurs at a line of B (5,880 of 5,880 non-degenerate cases, all 8,190 letters); far sides change only at a receiving atom's cut lines when R is one of six relations (504 cases), as with the removal's side alone. A free relation passes through a closed Fano atom (182 of 182). Hence acts-as-one holds for whether creation occurs, for every Fano atom of every knot space; far side by far side it holds except at a receiving atom's cut lines whose relation has six patterns, and without exception whenever only Fano atoms lie between, so on every Fano tree. Deep points behind B's own other elements are not bounded this way: with every relation their sides allow they can add creation at intact lines when R is free or not-all-equal (56 of 980 cases, one slot order), though they do not depend on the removed line.",
